    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Make an eight zero eight base."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Set oscillator 1 to a sine wave (wavetable position 0 on basic shapes) and transpose down 1 octave (-12 semitones) for the deep sub foundation. Set envelope 1 to instant attack (0s), zero sustain (0%), and a long decay around 2-3 seconds for the classic 808 tail that fades out smoothly."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Done."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Add a pitch envelope by routing envelope 2 to oscillator 1 pitch with a very short decay (0.05s) and moderate amount \u2014 this creates the characteristic 'punch' transient at the start of the hit. Add subtle saturation/soft distortion at low drive (15-25%) to give the sine wave some harmonic presence and help it translate on smaller speakers."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Done."
    },
