      "role": "user",
      "content": "<conversation_history>\nuser: Make an eight zero eight base.\nuser: Set oscillator 1 to a sine wave (wavetable position 0 on basic shapes) and transpose down 1 octave (-12 semitones) for the deep sub foundation. Set envelope 1 to instant attack (0s), zero sustain (0%), and a long decay around 2-3 seconds for the classic 808 tail that fades out smoothly.\nassistant: Done.\nuser: Add a pitch envelope by routing envelope 2 to oscillator 1 pitch with a very short decay (0.05s) and moderate amount \u2014 this creates the characteristic 'punch' transient at the start of the hit. Add subtle saturation/soft distortion at low drive (15-25%) to give the sine wave some harmonic presence and help it translate on smaller speakers.\nassistant: Done.\nuser: MAKE A SNARE DRUM SOUND\nuser: Enable oscillator 2 with a triangle wave, transpose up 1 octave (+12 semitones) for the tonal body of the snare. Set envelope 1 decay shorter (around 0.15-0.2s) for a snappier, more percussive hit.\nassistant: Done.\nuser: Enable the sampler with white noise for the snare's characteristic crack. Set sample level around 60-70% and route it through the same envelope 1 for unified decay.\nassistant: Done.\nuser: Keep the pitch envelope (env 2 to osc 1 pitch) but shorten the decay further (around 0.03s) for a tighter pitch drop that adds attack punch. Adjust modulation amount to around 20-25%. Increase distortion drive slightly (around 8-12) to add grit and help both the tonal and noise elements blend together with more presence.\nassistant: Done.\nuser: MAKE IT MORE SNAREY\nuser: Shorten envelope 1 decay to around 0.12-0.15s for a tighter, snappier transient. Reduce release to around 0.1s so the sound cuts off cleanly.\nassistant: Done.\nuser: Increase the noise (sampler) level to around 85-90% to bring out more of the characteristic snare crack and rattle. The noise should be more prominent than the tonal body.\nassistant: Done.\nuser: Enable filter 1 as a high-pass filter with cutoff around 40-50 to remove low-end mud from the snare and let the crack cut through. Route the sampler through this filter. Increase distortion drive to around 15-20 to add more aggression and help the transient bite harder.\nassistant: Done.\nuser: USE OSC 3 TO MAKE A DREAMY KEYYS PAD WHICH ALSO PLAYS AT THE SAME TIME AS THE SNARE (DNT REMOVE THE SNARE WITH OSC 1 AND 2)\nuser: Enable oscillator 3 with a sawtooth wave (wavetable position around 0.75 on basic shapes), add 4 unison voices with moderate detune (around 0.3) for lush width. Set level around 50-60% so it doesn't overpower the snare.\nassistant: Done.\n</conversation_history>\n\n<current_preset>\n{\"author\":\"\",\"comments\":\"\",\"macro1\":\"MACRO 1\",\"macro2\":\"MACRO 2\",\"macro3\":\"MACRO 3\",\"macro4\":\"MACRO 4\",\"preset_name\":\"Snappy Snare Drum\",\"preset_style\":\"\",\"settings\":{\"beats_per_minute\":2.0,\"bypass\":0.0,\"chorus_cutoff\":60.0,\"chorus_delay_1\":-9.0,\"chorus_delay_2\":-7.0,\"chorus_dry_wet\":0.5,\"chorus_feedback\":0.4000000059604645,\"chorus_frequency\":-3.0,\"chorus_mod_depth\":0.5,\"chorus_on\":0.0,\"chorus_spread\":1.0,\"chorus_sync\":1.0,\"chorus_tempo\":4.0,\"chorus_voices\":4.0,\"compressor_attack\":0.5,\"compressor_band_gain\":11.699999809265137,\"compressor_band_lower_ratio\":0.800000011920929,\"compressor_band_lower_threshold\":-36.0,\"compressor_band_upper_ratio\":0.8569999933242798,\"compressor_band_upper_threshold\":-25.0,\"compressor_enabled_bands\":0.0,\"compressor_high_gain\":16.299999237060547,\"compressor_high_lower_ratio\":0.800000011920929,\"compressor_high_lower_threshold\":-35.0,\"compressor_high_upper_ratio\":1.0,\"compressor_high_upper_threshold\":-30.0,\"compressor_low_gain\":16.299999237060547,\"compressor_low_lower_ratio\":0.800000011920929,\"compressor_low_lower_threshold\":-35.0,\"compressor_low_upper_ratio\":0.8999999761581421,\"compressor_low_upper_threshold\":-28.0,\"compressor_mix\":1.0,\"compressor_on\":0.0,\"compressor_release\":0.5,\"delay_a